.TH MKNODAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
mknodat \- Linux x86-64 syscall 259
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B int mknodat(int directory, const char* path, mode_t mode, unsigned int device);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a special file relative to a directory. The device argument is the raw Linux kernel encoding, not libc dev_t.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mknodat (2)
